Review: De‐escalation of antimicrobial treatment for adults with sepsis, severe sepsis or septic shock
Total studies to screen: 20

SELECTION CRITERIA:
We planned to include randomized controlled trials (RCTs) comparing de‐escalation (based on culture results) versus 
standard therapy for adults with sepsis, severe sepsis or septic shock. The primary outcome was mortality (at 28 days, 
hospital discharge or at the end of the follow‐up period). Studies including patients initially treated with an 
empirical but not adequate antimicrobial therapy were not considered for inclusion.

INSTRUCTIONS: For each study below, decide INCLUDE or EXCLUDE.
Return exactly one decision object per study; do not omit excluded studies, do not summarize exclusions in bulk, and do 
not return only included studies.
