│ "abstract": "Antibiotic de-escalation is a mechanism whereby the provision of effective initial antibiotic treatment │
│ is achieved while avoiding unnecessary antibiotic use that would promote the development of resistance. It is a key  │
│ element within antimicrobial stewardship programs and treatment paradigms for serious sepsis. The embodiment of      │
