METHODS This is a multicenter observational cohort study performed in five private and public, mixed ICUs from two      
different regions of Brazil. We prospectively followed 1383 adult patients consecutively admitted to those ICUs from May
2001 to January 2002, until their discharge, 28th day of stay, or death. For all patients we collected the following    
data at ICU admission: age, gender, hospital and ICU admission diagnosis, APACHE II score, and associated underlying    
