streptococci, (3) β-lactam-sensitive (a) Escherichia coli, and (b) Klebsiella species. The efficacy of appropriate 
initial empirical antimicrobial therapy, the performance of de-escalated pathogen-directed therapy, and the safety and 
efficacy of de-escalated therapy were evaluated. RESULTS Among 270 appropriately treated patients, 16 (6%) died, versus 
